-- The Bride v2 · red, yellow and black only. No text, no cream. Fan concept, not for sale.
create a card called the-bride-v2-closeup from stainless, seed 1973.

define a katana with $size 600 as:
  draw a shape called blade from 0 $size * -0.015 to $size * 0.3 $size * -0.025 to $size * 0.55 $size * -0.036 to $size * 0.8 $size * -0.052 to $size * 0.56 $size * -0.01 to $size * 0.3 $size * 0.003 to 0 $size * 0.015.
  draw an ellipse called guard, $size * 0.04 by $size * 0.13, at $size * -0.013 0.
  draw a rectangle called grip, $size * 0.26 by $size * 0.048, corners $size * 0.01, at $size * -0.167 0.
  draw a circle called pommel, $size * 0.024 big, at $size * -0.31 0.
end.

make the window 826 by 1415, at 207 207.

-- the bezel: a thick red frame with a black line inside it
draw a rectangle called inner-line, 826 by 1415, corners 8, hollow, 12 wide, at 620 914.

-- katana pattern running down both sides of the bezel
place 4 katanas called edge-l from 152 230, 390 apart, down, size 340, turned 90.
place 4 katanas called edge-r from 1088 400, 390 apart, down, size 340, turned -90.

-- the back checker
draw a rectangle called squares, 40 by 40, at 100 100.
copy the squares 14 times, 80 apart.
copy the squares 21 times, 80 apart, down.
copy the squares, by 40 40, called squares-2.

define $edge as:
  enamel its blade in yellow.
  enamel its guard and its grip and its pommel in black.
end.

on the front.
enamel the card in red.
print @bride-closeup.jpg in the window, focused at 0.5 0.5.
enamel the inner-line in black.
use $edge on the edge-l-1 and the edge-l-2 and the edge-l-3 and the edge-l-4 and the edge-r-1 and the edge-r-2 and the edge-r-3 and the edge-r-4.

on the back.
enamel the card in red.
enamel the window in yellow.
enamel the squares within the window in red.
enamel the squares-2 within the window in black.
enamel the inner-line in black.
use $edge on the edge-l-1 and the edge-l-2 and the edge-l-3 and the edge-l-4 and the edge-r-1 and the edge-r-2 and the edge-r-3 and the edge-r-4.
